<title>SWITZERLAND: Kohl - Germany doing all it can to meet EMU goals.</title>
<headline>Kohl - Germany doing all it can to meet EMU goals.</headline>
<dateline>INTERLAKEN, Switzerland 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany is doing all it can to meet the targets for EMU membership and the timetable set out in the Maastricht Treaty, German Chancellor Helmut Kohl said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;Germany will do everything to meet both the Maastricht criteria and timetable,&quot; Kohl said in an address to bankers at Interlaken.</p>
<p>Kohl went on to say that he thought EMU without Germany and other large countries would be hard to imagine.</p>
<p>--Catherine O'Mahoney, Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
